-- title:
--   Lemma 3.10 — $\lambda$-weighted descent inequality for Algorithm 2
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ players have convex compact sets $X_i\subseteq\mathbb R^{n_i}$ ($n_i\ge1$) with nonempty interior and $\nu_i$-self-concordant barriers $R_i$; let $\lambda_i>0$, $\beta>0$ and $n=\sum_in_i$. Let the iterates $x^t$ of Algorithm 2 be generated from rewards with $|u_i(x)|\le L$ for all $x\in X$ and a non-increasing step size with $0<\eta_t\le\frac1{2nL}$. Then for every realization of the directions on the unit spheres, every round $t\ge1$ and every $p$ with $p_i\in X_i$,
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   &\sum_i\lambda_iD_{R_i}(p_i,x_i^{t+1})+\frac{\eta_{t+1}\beta(t+1)}2\Big(\sum_i\|x_i^{t+1}-p_i\|^2\Big)\\
--   &\quad\le\sum_i\lambda_iD_{R_i}(p_i,x_i^t)+\frac{\eta_t\beta(t+1)}2\Big(\sum_i\|x_i^t-p_i\|^2\Big)+2\eta_t^2\Big(\sum_i\lambda_i\|A_i^t\hat v_i^t\|^2\Big)+\eta_t\Big(\sum_i\lambda_i\langle\hat v_i^t,x_i^t-p_i\rangle\Big).
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   This is the potential inequality that the proof of Theorem 3.8 takes in conditional expectation and telescopes.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: rewards of a (β, {λᵢ})-strongly monotone smooth concave game (standing assumption of §3.4) → arbitrary functions uᵢ with |uᵢ(x)| ≤ L on X; reason: the inequality uses only |uᵢ(x̂ᵗ)| ≤ L (Appendix E via Lemma 2.12); the source's games are instances
--   - reading: n in 0 < ηₜ ≤ 1/(2nL) → n = Σᵢ nᵢ; reason: Appendix E, p.33: "Since n = Σ_{i∈N} nᵢ in the multi-agent setting"
--   - encoding: random directions zᵢᵗ ∼ Sⁿⁱ → every family of directions with ‖zᵢᵗ‖ = 1 (pathwise); reason: the lemma is an inequality for each realization of the draws
--   - encoding: dimensions nᵢ, sets Xᵢ, weights λᵢ → nᵢ ≥ 1, int Xᵢ nonempty, λᵢ > 0; reason: Sⁿⁱ is empty for nᵢ = 0; Rᵢ : int(Xᵢ) → ℝ and the initialization need int Xᵢ ≠ ∅; Algorithm 2 takes λᵢ > 0 as input
--   - encoding: 0 < ηₜ ≤ 1/(2nL) → the same with Lean's 1/0 = 0, so L = 0 makes the hypothesis unsatisfiable; reason: 1/(2nL) is undefined at L = 0; only that undefined case is excluded
--   - encoding: argmin over Xᵢ in (3.3) and in the initialization → argmin over int Xᵢ; reason: the objectives contain Rᵢ, defined on int Xᵢ only
-- source:
--   Ba, Lin, Zhang & Zhou, Doubly Optimal No-Regret Online Learning in Strongly Monotone Games with Bandit Feedback, arXiv:2112.02856v4, Lemma 3.10, p.15; Algorithm 2, p.15; (3.3), p.14; Appendix E, p.33

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_EntropicBarrier_Universal_SelfConcordantBarrier
import Definitions.Def_DoublyOptBandit_Algorithm2

open scoped InnerProductSpace

namespace DoublyOptBandit

/-- **Lemma 3.10** (descent inequality for Algorithm 2; Ba, Lin, Zhang & Zhou,
arXiv:2112.02856v4, Lemma 3.10, p.15). Let each `Xᵢ ⊆ ℝ^{nᵢ}` be convex and compact with nonempty
interior, `Rᵢ` a `νᵢ`-self-concordant barrier for `Xᵢ`, `λᵢ > 0`, `β > 0`, and let the iterates
`xᵗ` be generated by Algorithm 2 from rewards with `|uᵢ(x)| ≤ L` on `X` and a non-increasing step
size with `0 < ηₜ ≤ 1/(2nL)`, `n = Σᵢ nᵢ`. Then for every realization of the directions `zᵢᵗ` on
the unit spheres, every round `t ≥ 1` and every `p` with `pᵢ ∈ Xᵢ`,
`Σᵢ λᵢD_{Rᵢ}(pᵢ, xᵢᵗ⁺¹) + (ηₜ₊₁β(t+1)/2)(Σᵢ ‖xᵢᵗ⁺¹ − pᵢ‖²) ≤ Σᵢ λᵢD_{Rᵢ}(pᵢ, xᵢᵗ) +
(ηₜβ(t+1)/2)(Σᵢ ‖xᵢᵗ − pᵢ‖²) + 2ηₜ²(Σᵢ λᵢ‖Aᵢᵗv̂ᵢᵗ‖²) + ηₜ(Σᵢ λᵢ⟨v̂ᵢᵗ, xᵢᵗ − pᵢ⟩)`.

**Formalization Note** Pathwise in the directions (`‖zᵢᵗ‖ = 1` for all `t, i`). The rewards are
arbitrary functions bounded by `L` on `X`; the game structure of §3.4 is not assumed. Note
`ηₜ₊₁` on the left and `ηₜ` on the right, as printed. `n = Σᵢ nᵢ` as in Appendix E, p.33; every
`nᵢ ≥ 1` (the unit sphere of `ℝ⁰` is empty). -/
theorem lemma_3_10 {N : ℕ} (n : Fin N → ℕ) (hn : ∀ i, 1 ≤ n i)
    (X : ∀ i, Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n i)))) (hXc : ∀ i, IsCompact (X i))
    (hXcv : ∀ i, Convex ℝ (X i)) (hXi : ∀ i, (interior (X i)).Nonempty)
    (R : ∀ i, EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n i)) → ℝ) (ν : Fin N → ℝ)
    (hR : ∀ i, EntropicBarrier.Universal.IsNuSelfConcordantBarrier (X i) (R i) (ν i))
    (lam : Fin N → ℝ) (hlam : ∀ i, 0 < lam i) (β : ℝ) (hβ : 0 < β) (L : ℝ)
    (u : Fin N → Joint n → ℝ) (hu : ∀ i, ∀ x ∈ jointSet X, |u i x| ≤ L) (η : ℕ → ℝ)
    (hη : ∀ t, 1 ≤ t → 0 < η t ∧ η t ≤ 1 / (2 * (∑ i, (n i : ℝ)) * L))
    (hηmono : ∀ t, 1 ≤ t → η (t + 1) ≤ η t)
    (z : ℕ → ∀ i, EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n i))) (hz : ∀ t i, ‖z t i‖ = 1)
    (t : ℕ) (ht : 1 ≤ t) (p : Joint n) (hp : p ∈ jointSet X) :
    ∑ i, lam i * BeckTeboulleMD.EMDA.bregman (R i) (p i) (alg2Iter X R u lam β η z (t + 1) i) +
        η (t + 1) * β * ((t : ℝ) + 1) / 2 *
          (∑ i, ‖alg2Iter X R u lam β η z (t + 1) i - p i‖ ^ 2) ≤
      ∑ i, lam i * BeckTeboulleMD.EMDA.bregman (R i) (p i) (alg2Iter X R u lam β η z t i) +
        η t * β * ((t : ℝ) + 1) / 2 * (∑ i, ‖alg2Iter X R u lam β η z t i - p i‖ ^ 2) +
        2 * η t ^ 2 * (∑ i, lam i *
          ‖Matrix.toEuclideanLin (alg2Scaling X R u lam β η z t i)
            (alg2Estimate X R u lam β η z t i)‖ ^ 2) +
        η t * (∑ i, lam i *
          ⟪alg2Estimate X R u lam β η z t i, alg2Iter X R u lam β η z t i - p i⟫_ℝ) := by sorry

end DoublyOptBandit
